# Server/core architecture
- Target: one Next.js/TypeScript-first application backed by Supabase, with server-side frontier-model integration. Durable worker execution is OPEN, not something to scaffold by habit.
- Never put provider/service credentials in client or direct model calls from browser.
- Keep pure validation, arithmetic and Study acceptance logic out of framework-specific route handlers; keep I/O and authorization on server boundaries.
- `hive-extract/1` is pack-free default. Extraction models yield untrusted candidate JSON; only independent verifier can accept observations.
- Study revision pointer is advanced atomically on successfully accepted revision. Reports and analyses pin revision, each Generate action has a unique run.
- Avoid new environment variables, feature flags, shadow pipelines, duplicate provider adapters and unnecessary packages.
- Consult `docs/HiveForYou-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/HiveForYou-REPOSITORY-STRUCTURE.md` and `docs/HiveForYou-DATA-MODEL.md`; do not invent file paths or migration status.
